        "knowledge_point": {
          "db_id": 17592186129283,
          "id": "091b8235-56d8-5a08-bc95-08c99772cfd8",
          "title": "Finding Regions Where a Transformation is Orientation-Preserving or Reversing"
        },
        "question": {
          ":question/id": "c1c5af5f-3f90-521d-ba99-86a57c026483",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\u27f6\\begin{bmatrix}\\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} \\\\ 4 v + 12\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202(x,y)}{\u2202(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\u27f6\\begin{bmatrix}\\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} \\\\ 4 v + 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202(x,y)}{\u2202(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(2 u + 2)\\cdot (4)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=8 u + 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 u + 8 &<0 \\\\ u < -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nu = -1\n$$\n\ndefines a vertical line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](/tmp/ca9837-templates-z7ii9jxi/17592186129283/plot-f1ac0c9f881ad97f2985.png)",
