        "question": {
          ":question/id": "4e9ca55b-d9dd-5ec6-b4fa-853cf18076a8",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\u27f6\\begin{bmatrix}{(u + 1)}^{2}-v \\\\ (u + 1)v+1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202(x,y)}{\u2202(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\u27f6\\begin{bmatrix}{(u + 1)}^{2}-v \\\\ (u + 1)v+1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202(x,y)}{\u2202(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\u2202x}{\u2202u} & \\frac{\u2202x}{\u2202v} \\\\ \\frac{\u2202y}{\u2202u} & \\frac{\u2202y}{\u2202v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2(u + 1) & -1 \\\\ v & (u + 1)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(u + 1)\\cdot (u + 1)-v\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{(u + 1)}^{2}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(u + 1)}^{2}+v & >0 \\\\ v & >-2{(u + 1)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-2{(u + 1)}^{2}\n$$\n\ndefines a parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(0,1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](/tmp/ca9837-templates-z7ii9jxi/17592186129283/plot-a12181bd65947a715711.png)",
